From: T531 Project <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ambient: require a light sensor before enabling auto brightness

SensorProxy may successfully accept ClaimLight without a populated ambient
light sensor. An unblank currently issues that claim whenever the ambient
brightness preference is enabled, even with HasAmbientLight=false. The
successful reply enables automatic brightness using an invalid zero-lux
reading and changes the hidden-auto slider into an offset control.

On SM-T531 / Phosh 0.58.0 with no ALS exposed, the actual GTK brightness
slider at 0/25/50/75/100 percent writes LP8556 levels 2/2/3/11/37 instead of
2/7/23/76/255. Its maximum is the zero-lux base 0.1 plus offset 0.5, not the
hardware maximum. Preserve the existing curve and brightness preference;
require sensor availability and an unblanked display for claims and auto
activation. Release a disappearing sensor and reconcile availability after
asynchronous replies, serializing calls to avoid stale or duplicate claims.

Cover absent sensors, normal appearance/disappearance, disappearance while
claiming and reappearance while releasing using the real ambient state
machine with delayed successful D-Bus replies. Upstream source copyrights
and authorship are retained.

Forwarded: not-yet
---
